# SPARK AppWorks Cursor Rules

默认用简体中文沟通。代码标识符、命令、路径和错误原文保持原文。

## Environment

- Node >= 20, pnpm >= 10. Verify with `node --version` and `pnpm --version` when environment issues are possible.
- Frontend dependencies: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.
- Java work under `spark-ai-server/` requires JDK 17+; pure frontend work skips Java.
- After `spark-ai-server/` changes, restart `pnpm run dev` (or the Spring Boot process on 8180); the Java backend has no HMR.
- Avoid slow commands unless explicitly needed: `pnpm run dev`, `pnpm run build`, and `cd spark-ai-server && mvn install`.

## Fast Verification

After code changes, prefer focused checks first:

- `pnpm run typecheck`
- `pnpm run lint`
- `pnpm run test`
- `pnpm run verify:rules` when touching architecture boundaries, AI codegen rules, docs governance, or VCM/LLM-visible comments.

## Package Boundaries

Dependency order is strict and acyclic:

`spark-utils <- spark-data <- spark-project-model <- spark-component <- spark-app`

- Cross-package imports must use `@spark-appworks/*` package names, never relative paths.
- `spark-utils`, `spark-data`, and `spark-project-model` must stay framework-free. Do not import `vue`, `vue-router`, `element-plus`, DOM globals, or UI framework APIs there.
- Business capability DI uses `sparkProvide` / `sparkConsume`. Vue `provide/inject` is only for infrastructure.

## Runtime Data Flow

The DataSet pipeline is one-way:

`pagedata.json -> parsePageData() -> DataSet -> usePageDataSet() -> PAGE_DATASET -> dataViewKey + dataMember + dataField -> DataView -> UI`

- Do not bypass with `pageData`, `$data`, raw renderer JSON normalization, or old member-joined keys.
- Never call `DataSet.destroy()` from `clearDataSet()`; DataSet instances are cached across navigation.
- `dataViewKey` format is `table@viewId` or `#scope@table@viewId`.
- `dataMember` examples: `rows`, `currentRow`, `aggregateResult`.
- `dataField` is an optional object-field path such as `customer.name`.

## Code Generation Behavior

Before generating or modifying production code, follow `docs/ai/AI_CODE_GENERATION_BEHAVIOR.en.md` and `docs/ai/ai-code-generation-behavior.md`.

Core rules:

- Do not default everything to `interface`.
- Prefer `contract -> base/default class -> concrete class -> necessary subclass` layering when an abstraction is justified.
- Use `interface` only for stable contracts, DTO/config/payload boundaries, cross-module capabilities, or multiple implementations.
- If there is one implementation, prefer a concrete class, named type, or plain function.
- Function signatures should have at most 3 positional parameters. Use a named options/command object for 4+ values.
- Do not put large anonymous object types, deep generics, or JSDoc inside parameter lists.
- Keep public exports converged. Avoid public `export *`.
- Comments explain contracts, constraints, priority, and risk; avoid obvious narration.

## Page Configuration

- Configuration first: prefer `rule.json`, `pagedata.json`, view metadata, and existing renderer capabilities.
- Use `script.js` only when configuration cannot express the behavior.
- Runtime page configs in `spark-ai-server/data/pages-config/` are the source of truth.
- Sandbox globals allowed in page `script.js`: `$page`, `$route`, `$dataSet`, `$query`, `SparkData`, `h`.
- Forbidden in page `script.js`: `$data`, ESM `import`, `window.xxx` globals, direct `ElMessage` / `ElMessageBox`, direct Vue Router imports.

## AI UI Assembly SOP

When constructing Spark UI nodes through AI tools:

1. Query payload specs first with `queryPayloads({})`, `queryPayloads({ category: 'container' })`, or `queryPayloads({ keyword: '...' })`.
2. For a selected component type, call `guidePayload({ key: '<component-type>' })`.
3. Build SparkNode JSON only from the returned legal schema.
4. Write with `pageDesign@nodeTree@addNode` or `pageDesign@nodeTree@addNodes`.

Never invent component props without reading the specs.

## Large Files

Do not directly edit generated or large metadata files:

- `packages/spark-ai/src/catalog/component-catalog.json`
- `spark-ai-server/data/component-metadata.json`

## Commit Format

Use `<type>(<scope>): <description>`.

Allowed scopes: `deps`, `docs`, `scripts`, `spark-data`, `spark-app`, `spark-ai`, `spark-component`, `spark-utils`, `spark-project-model`.
